  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the publication of her memoir titled 'Belonging: A Journey of Love,' Sonia Gandhi has faced significant political and legal backlash. The book provides personal reflections on her life in Indian politics and the experiences of her family, including the security situation surrounding Rajiv Gandhi. Recently, the family of Vinayak Damodar Savarkar issued a legal notice, citing concerns over how he is depicted in the text. This development adds to a series of controversies involving political leaders who have criticized the memoir, with some officials in Maharashtra demanding a ban on the book. Other political factions have characterized the memoir as a platform that exposes historical actions of the Congress party. The ongoing discourse reflects the polarized reception of the former Congress leader's autobiography across the Indian political landscape.",
